# TypeScript Rules

## Type Safety Strategy

### Auto-Generated API Types

- **Primary approach**: Generate types from OpenAPI/GraphQL schema
- Generated types live in `lib/api/generated/`
- Export from `lib/api/index.ts` for use across app
- See `scripts/generate-api-types.md` for setup

### Manual Types

- Global types in `types/` folder
- Feature-specific types in `features/{feature}/types/`
- Use `types/common.ts` for shared entity types

### Type Organization

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Export types from feature modules
// features/auth/types/index.ts
export interface User { /* ... */ }
export interface LoginRequest { /* ... */ }

// ✅ CORRECT: Export common types globally
// types/common.ts
export interface BaseEntity { /* ... */ }
```

## Type Inference

- Use `z.infer<typeof schema>` for Zod schema types
- Use `ReturnType<typeof function>` when appropriate
- Prefer explicit types for public APIs, inference for internals

## Strict TypeScript

- Project uses **strict mode** - all rules enabled
- Never use `any` - use `unknown` if type is truly unknown
- Use type assertions sparingly - prefer type guards
